---
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ClosingCta from '../components/ClosingCta.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbList, serviceNode } from '../lib/schema';
import { SITE_URL, SERVICE_AREA_PLACES } from '../site';
const title = 'Business Advisory in Northern Virginia | Danny McGiffin';
const description = 'Independent business advisory, operating-model design, and business systems work for owners and leaders in Northern Virginia. Based in Herndon.';
const pageUrl = `${SITE_URL}/northern-virginia-ai-workflow-automation/`;
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} structuredData={[breadcrumbList([{name:'Home',url:`${SITE_URL}/`},{name:'Northern Virginia',url:pageUrl}]),serviceNode({id:`${pageUrl}#service`,name:'Business advisory and operating-model design',description,url:pageUrl,areaServed:SERVICE_AREA_PLACES})]}>
  <SiteHeader /><main id="main-content"><header class="page-intro section-dark"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Herndon / Northern Virginia</p><h1>Business problems<br />don’t respect<br /><em>department boundaries.</em></h1><p class="intro-deck">Independent business advisory and design for owners and leaders in Northern Virginia and the Washington, DC area.</p></div></header>
  <article class="prose service-prose shell"><h2>When the answer isn’t obvious.</h2><p>I’m Danny McGiffin, an independent business advisor and designer based in Herndon. I work on consequential problems that cross strategy, operations, people, and systems.</p><p>The owner has become the bottleneck. The strategy and the way the company runs no longer fit. Leadership sees the same problem and reaches three different conclusions. A major system is already in motion, but nobody is sure it’s the right answer.</p><p>You don’t have to translate that into an automation project before we talk.</p><h2>Advice, design, and help making it real.</h2><p>I help leadership understand what is happening, evaluate options, and make a decision. When something needs redesigning, I work through the operating model, responsibilities, decision rights, business systems, and experience of the people involved.</p><p>When implementation is useful, I can help put the design into practice through systems, software, integrations, automation, documentation, and hands-on work. Technology is one of the tools available. It isn’t the starting point.</p><h2>Sometimes the work is stopping the wrong project.</h2><p>For a PE-backed distributor, I helped identify that an enterprise ERP couldn’t naturally represent the relationships at the heart of its business. Once we made the tradeoff clear, the CEO canceled the implementation. I designed an alternative architecture around the systems already in use.</p><p>For a professional-services firm, the problem was different: it wanted its commercial practices to collaborate in the federal market, but their incentives discouraged it. I redesigned the operating model around ownership and an enabling Federal function.</p><p><a href="/about/">Read those accounts and more about my work.</a></p><h2>Close enough to see the real work.</h2><p>Herndon is home base. I work across Northern Virginia and the Washington, DC area, including Reston, Chantilly, Fairfax, Tysons, McLean, Vienna, Ashburn, Leesburg, Arlington, and Alexandria, as well as Loudoun and Fairfax counties.</p><p>Some work is on site; some is remote. The choice depends on what we need to understand and who needs to be involved. Those are service areas, not a list of offices.</p><h2>A useful fit.</h2><p>This work is for owners, executives, and senior operators at founder-led or privately held businesses with meaningful stakes and a willingness to examine what is actually happening.</p><p>We need access to the people, decisions, and work involved. You don’t need a predetermined solution. We can begin with an important question.</p></article><ClosingCta /></main><SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
